  "slug": "screening-web-server-dda8",
  "summary": "Public web servers now expose predictors for kinase, CYP450, and virtual screening tasks, with new ADME and permeability preprints following.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is packaging predictive models as accessible, task-specific web tools for drug discovery triage. DeepKinomeWeb uses a deep learning regression model to predict kinase-inhibitor affinities and visualize panel-level selectivity. DeepCYP applies a multi-task graph neural network to CYP450 pathway-site and product prediction across nine isoforms, reported as outperforming FAME3. PLATE-VS curates assay data, structures, and property-matched decoys into virtual screening datasets. Preprints extend this toward ADME and CNS endpoints: PredHLM uses XGBoost on RDKit descriptors for liver microsome half-life across 11,790 compounds with SHAP interpretation, and BBBP_Atlas applies a structure-aware graph model to blood-brain barrier permeability. The repurposing pipeline is a distinct workflow. What is new is interpretability paired with public deployment, though comparative benefit beyond the FAME3 comparison is not established.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-13"
}
